# Tool Development boundary declaration

The presence of this file marks the tree as a **Tool Development** tree: the reusable
Agentic AI Testing Platform, with **no project-owned data tracked**.

    git ls-files platform_core_data     ->     must be EMPTY

Enforced by `scripts/verifyBranchBoundary.js` (`npm run verify:boundary`, and `prepack`).

## Why a file and not a branch name

The branches most likely to reintroduce project data are the `feature/*` branches cut
*from* `tool-development` — a branch-name check would not cover them, and would silently
disable itself on a detached HEAD. This declaration is inherited by anything branched from
here, so the check follows the work rather than the label.

## What this means in practice

| Branch | Declaration | `platform_core_data` |
|---|---|---|
| `tool-development` and anything cut from it | present | **zero tracked files** |
| `platform-testing` and anything cut from it | absent | tracked, deliberately |

`platform_core_data/` may still exist **on disk** here — `git rm --cached` untracks without
deleting — so a working copy that also does dogfooding keeps its data. It is simply not part
of this branch's tree.

## Direction of change

```text
feature/*  ->  tool-development  ->  platform-testing
```

Tool source flows down. Project evidence never flows back. If a Tool fix is made while on
`platform-testing`, promote only the Tool-owned files — never merge that branch backward.

**Do not delete this file to make a check pass.** Deleting it removes the invariant, not the
violation.
